course: dictionary
lesson: 5558
title: Length
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Length is a noun, and its meaning depends on the words around it. Length is how long something is from one end to the other, like the length of a pencil or a rope. You can also look at how long something lasts. The length of a film is how long it runs.
explain: Look for clues. «Then he went in goal for the Year 3s' lunchtime match, dived full length in the mud and saved a penalty.» Full length here must mean his whole body stretched out flat, because that is what a goalkeeper does when diving.
explain: Length can also mean a piece of something, as in a length of rope. «At length» means for a long time, or at last. So if someone waits at length, they have waited a long time, or they finally did something.
fact: Length is measured in centimetres (cm), metres (m) or kilometres (km).
fact: In a swimming pool, a length is the distance from one end to the other, so swimming ten lengths means swimming from one end to the other ten times.
fact: In maths, length is one side of a rectangle. Length × width gives the area.
fact: «Length» can mean how long something lasts, as in the length of a film.
fact: «At length» means for a long time, or at last.
exercise: «Then he went in goal for the Year 3s' lunchtime match, dived full length in the mud and saved a penalty.» What does full length mean here? | *Stretched out flat, from head to toe | Quickly, like a race | Half way across the pitch | Very long, like a big bus
exercise: What units is length measured in? | Hours and minutes | Kilograms and grams | Litres and millilitres | *Centimetres, metres and kilometres
exercise: «We waited at length for the bus, and then at last it came.» What does at length mean in this sentence? | In the middle of the road | *For a long time, or at last | Very quietly | For a short time only
test: A rectangle has a length of 8 cm and a width of 5 cm. What is its area? | 26 square centimetres | *40 square centimetres | 80 centimetres | 13 square centimetres
test: The length of the film is two hours. What does length mean here? | A piece of rope | *How long the film lasts | The width of the screen | The distance from the cinema to home
exam: Which sentence uses length to mean a piece of something? | *She cut a length of ribbon for the present | The film's length was two hours | He swam ten lengths of the pool | The length of the desk is one metre
